# Nexus Estate API agent rules

Read `docs/developer.rules.md` before changing code. It is the canonical
architecture document; these are the non-negotiable agent gates.

## Feature-based module architecture

- All work is scoped to `nexus-estate-api`.
- `src/modules/<module>/` is a bounded context. Its direct children must be
  named business features such as `account`, `authentication`, `registration`,
  `authorization`, `property`, `provider-review`, `asset`, or
  `legacy-global`.
- The module root may contain only its composition files (`<module>.module.ts`
  and its sidecar). Business code belongs in a feature directory.
- Do not create module-root technical layers: `controllers`, `services`,
  `repositories`, `models`, `entities`, `dto`, `guards`, `strategies`,
  `helpers`, `enums`, `type`, `errors`, `decorators`, `constants`, or
  `permissions`.
- Inside every feature, keep the normal layer-based folders: `controllers/`,
  `services/`, `repositories/`, `entities/`, `dto/`, `guards/`, `strategies/`,
  `helpers/`, `errors/`, `constants/`, and `types/`. The files in those layers
  must belong to that feature. Do not flatten production files directly into a
  feature root except its composition file. Only feature-owned `migrations/`
  and explicit `data-migrations/` lifecycle folders are allowed as additional
  nested technical folders.
- If a feature grows across independent lifecycles, split it into named
  business features. Do not solve that growth with `services/` or `utils/`.
- `src/common`, `src/services/abstraction-services`, `src/utils`, and
  `src/database` are cross-cutting/infrastructure boundaries; do not move
  domain behavior there merely to avoid choosing a feature owner.
- Customer, Provider, Administration, Estate, and legacy RBAC boundaries must
  follow the ownership and realm rules in `docs/developer.rules.md`. New
  runtime code must not use global RBAC semantics.

## Mandatory TypeScript sidecar tests

- Every production TypeScript file under `src/` (`*.ts`) MUST have exactly one
  colocated test sidecar beside it: either `<name>.spec.ts` or `<name>.test.ts`,
  never both.
- The sidecar must import the file under test and protect its public behavior,
  exported contract, metadata, or invariants. Indirect coverage is insufficient.
- `*.spec.ts`, `*.test.ts`, E2E tests, and integration tests are test artifacts
  and are exempt from recursively requiring another sidecar.
- New or modified source is incomplete until its sidecar covers normal behavior,
  invalid input/error behavior, boundary conditions, and applicable security or
  domain invariants. Empty existence-only tests are not accepted.
- This applies to entities, constants, enums, registries, DTOs, decorators,
  modules, controllers, guards, repositories, services, migrations, scripts,
  barrels, and types.
- `src/source-sidecar-coverage.spec.ts` is a hard gate. Run it before handoff.

## Mandatory full-flow feature tests

- Every business capability, feature, or user-visible API workflow needs a
  full-flow spec under the existing `test/` directory:
  `test/<module>/<feature>.spec.ts`.
- Do not create a parallel top-level `tests/` directory. Existing
  `test/integration/` remains valid for infrastructure/migration suites.
- Exercise the real application and persistence boundary appropriate to the
  feature (`HTTP/module -> guards -> controller -> service -> repository/
  database`). Unit mocks do not replace full-flow coverage.
- Cover happy path, invalid input, unauthenticated/forbidden access, ownership
  or scope violations, state-transition failures, duplicate/idempotency,
  rollback/atomicity, and relevant concurrency/revocation cases.
- Add a regression case for every discovered or fixed bug, including boundary
  values and alternative states.

## Delivery gates

- Preserve user changes and do not perform destructive broad resets.
- Use feature paths in imports; stale imports such as `../services/...`,
  `../models/...`, or `../controllers/...` are architecture violations.
- Before declaring completion, run the sidecar inventory, `npm run typecheck`,
  lint, relevant unit tests, and relevant `test/` full-flow/integration suites.
- For schema changes, run migration verification against the configured Nexus
  Estate PostgreSQL environment. If unavailable, report the limitation rather
  than using another project's database.
